From aa75d2a346b18fb8be9bbb9c321ad7b15f5088d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:49:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): one tool preview, a full points table, plain words
 on the profile page

The Profile tab of the tool editor has no second side view. The one
to-scale preview draws the draft of the tab: a drawn holder as the bands
that the collision check sweeps, a drawn cutter as the steel outline.

The points table keeps a least height of 150 px. egui gave the nested
scroll area only the space left in the view, so a table low on the page
showed about two rows. The grid has no 40 px least column width, so the
remove buttons stay in a narrow pane. The tab row and the file buttons
wrap.

The page says "In use: ..." in place of "landed", and the table headers
and the holder line use plain words.

Refs #2007

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
